  "analysis_type": "descriptive",
  "question": "For four paper-named GRCm39 loci, how do paired-library RNA and common-region fragment changes differ in two GSE329778 contrasts, and how sensitive are they to region, depth weighting, prior RNA-QC selection and explicit source-record counting definition?",
  "decision": "Execute every eligible fixed Q4a case and retain source/locus/subset holds; describe paired measurements without a regulatory-memory or population inference. Exact author replay and original state-resolved Q4 remain held.",
  "strongest_rival": "Composition, lineage/genotype/sorting selection, sparse counts, processing and annotation-defined region choice can explain nonparallel RNA/fragment patterns without regulatory priming. Mouse/preparation independence and author state maps remain unverified.",
  "discriminator": "Same exact positive-RNA/nuclear-fragment barcode sets for both modalities; compare source-defined TSS-window unions with gene bodies, pooled with equal-barcode summaries, and prior RNA-QC intersection. These distinguish measurement/selection sensitivity, not biological mechanism or cell-state effects. Additionally compare strand-labelled source records with coordinate/barcode groups using internally consistent numerators and denominators; neither definition certifies physical molecules.",
  "evidence_refs": [
    "Research Article/ungated_arozamena_2026_inflammatory_memory/ACCESSIBILITY_EXTENSION_BRIEF.md",
